Actually, the simplest and most effective micro-optimization for such a small function is to reduce the number of dereferences. Since `profile` is used twice, storing it in a local variable avoids one dereference in the common case where profile is non-NULL:

```cpp
#include <cstddef>

FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    auto p = profile;
    if (p == nullptr) return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    if (profileIndex >= p->numFields) return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```

